# Pattern: Checkpoint & Restore

Purpose:
  Enable chain recovery by saving state after each stage.
  If chain fails, resume from last successful checkpoint
  instead of starting over. Ensures no work is lost.

## Checkpoint Strategy

Checkpoint Trigger:
  - After each successful stage completion
  - Before stage with high failure risk (C1, DEP1)
  - On human approval gates
  - Periodic (every N stages)

Checkpoint Content:
  - Chain execution ID
  - Current stage
  - Completed stages list
  - Stage outputs (compressed)
  - Token usage per stage
  - Decision state
  - Timestamp
  - Hash for integrity

Checkpoint Storage:
  .runtime/checkpoints/
    <chain-id>/
      checkpoint-<stage>.json
      manifest.json

Checkpoint Retention:
  - Keep last 10 checkpoints per chain
  - Delete after successful chain completion
  - Archive old checkpoints to .runtime/archive/

## Restore Strategy

Restore Trigger:
  - Chain failure detected
  - User requests /sdd-resume
  - System detects incomplete chain

Restore Process:
  1. Load latest checkpoint
  2. Verify checkpoint integrity (hash)
  3. Identify last successful stage
  4. Resume from next stage
  5. Skip completed stages
  6. Continue chain execution

Restore Validation:
  - Checkpoint hash matches
  - Stage outputs are valid
  - Dependencies are met
  - No conflicting state

## State Recovery

State Backup:
  - Backup .sdd/project/state/ before each stage
  - Store in checkpoint
  - Restore on failure

State Rollback:
  - If stage fails, rollback to checkpoint state
  - Discard partial outputs
  - Resume from checkpoint

## Idempotency

Idempotent Stages:
  - P1: Can re-run with same prompt
  - D1: Can re-run with same inputs
  - S1: Can re-run with same decisions
  - C1: Can re-run with same .sdd/ (overwrites code)
  - R1: Can re-run review
  - DEP1: Cannot re-run (production deployment)

Idempotency Keys:
  - Prompt hash for P1
  - Decision hash for D1
  - .sdd/ state hash for S1
  - Template hash for C1

## Recovery Metrics

Track:
  - Checkpoint frequency
  - Restore frequency
  - Time saved by restore
  - Failure rate per stage
  - Recovery success rate

## Commands

/sdd-checkpoint:
  Create manual checkpoint
  Usage: /sdd-checkpoint --name=<name>

/sdd-resume:
  Resume from last checkpoint
  Usage: /sdd-resume --chain=<chain-id>

/sdd-checkpoints:
  List available checkpoints
  Usage: /sdd-checkpoints --chain=<chain-id>

State: +
